00:05:08.520 --> 00:05:13.080
and exploring these loops and so on, one of the things we found from using

87
00:05:13.120 --> 00:05:17.200
a variety of different code review tools was they didn't quite fit

88
00:05:17.640 --> 00:05:23.360
the Tessl philosophy of the factory being composed of skills and loops.

89
00:05:23.400 --> 00:05:27.720
We found that a lot of our tools we were using were black boxes.

90
00:05:27.760 --> 00:05:30.760
There was no way to build a self-improvement loop on them.

91
00:05:30.760 --> 00:05:34.080
We were discovering all these issues with code generation

92
00:05:34.080 --> 00:05:37.440
and context, and creating skills and plugins to help address that.

93
00:05:37.440 --> 00:05:40.920
But our code review is still the same old code review we were using.

94
00:05:40.960 --> 00:05:44.520
And so we were increasingly thinking about how to make code review

95
00:05:44.760 --> 00:05:47.760
a part of the context, a part of the

96
00:05:47.880 --> 00:05:52.520
the Tessl structure that can be self improved as we go along.

97
00:05:52.880 --> 00:05:56.720
And with that, that meant we ended up building our own code review.

98
00:05:56.840 --> 00:06:00.360
We ran it over several months and built it up over time

99
00:06:00.360 --> 00:06:04.800
to address our needs and to make it fit the factory native way of thinking.

